WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.670
- [Narrator] There's a
lot of international mail

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.053
that flows to a small
nation in Western Africa.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.190
The mail is addressed to an address

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.953
that should be right here
along this main street.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.890
But I asked my friends to
go there and check it out,

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.861
and he didn't find anything.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.570
- I've been looking for 80 Broad Street.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.860
I'm gonna say that 80
Broad Street doesn't exist.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.450
- [Narrator] Instead, the mail
that is addressed to go here

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.450
is actually brought to a building
down the road, right here.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.733
- Right here,

00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:45.760
this building is where all
LISCR bills are forwarded,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.100
from the building that doesn't
exist on 80 Broad Street.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.750
- [Narrator] From there,
the mail is scanned

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.840
and sent electronically
thousands of miles away

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.820
to a nondescript office building
outside of Washington, DC,

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.570
it's actually right near my
house in Northern Virginia.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.500
- Henry check out this random building.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.528
Does this building looks
super boring to you?

00:01:06.528 --> 00:01:07.361
- Ooh.

00:01:07.361 --> 00:01:09.050
- This building is right near our house.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:12.623
I guess I expected something
a little bit more interesting.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.000
- [Narrator] This process
is a part of a secretive web

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.450
of corporate secrecy.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.720
It's a web that is built off
of years of strange connections

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.660
between the United States
and the country of Liberia,

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:29.660
a nation invented by a group
of Americans here in Virginia.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.320
This is how the US stashed its secrets

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.943
off the coast of West Africa.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:39.703
- In this building,

00:01:39.703 --> 00:01:42.200
there is a bunch of mail that comes from

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.290
a little country in West Africa,

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.120
and it gets sent to this
building near our house.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.640
Does that seem kind of weird to you?

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.605
- Yes, what do they do with it?

00:01:50.605 --> 00:01:51.573
(chuckles)

00:01:51.573 --> 00:01:53.953
- That's what I wanna figure out here.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.500
So, let's say I wanna start
an international corporation

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.430
and start doing business abroad.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:01.830
I live here in the United States,

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.930
so naturally I would wanna
start my company here in the US,

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:07.360
but when I asked the
internet how to do this,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.233
I get a bunch of ads that look like this.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.530
Even though my office would be here

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.370
in Washington, DC in the United States,

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:17.710
the internet is telling me that on paper,

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:21.320
I should set up my corporation
in one of these random,

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.510
small countries around the world.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.310
Places like the British
Virgin islands, or Mauritius,

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:29.840
or Belize, Gibraltar, Malta,
the Seychelles Islands,

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.740
wait, the Seychelles like
that tiny Island nation

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.430
in the middle of the Indian ocean,

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.330
that has like less than a
hundred thousand people.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.760
It's like 40 hours of flying to get there,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.667
why would I wanna set up my
business in the Seychelles?

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:46.250
(upbeat music)

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:48.770
Here's why.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:51.100
If I set up my corporation on paper,

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.020
in the British Virgin
islands or the Seychelles,

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.720
suddenly I actually don't
have to pay very much taxes,

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:57.630
if any at all.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.630
My new corporation now won't have

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:02.650
to actually obey any of the corporate laws

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:03.950
here in the United States,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.200
which require you to publish
all sorts of information

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.460
about your finances,

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.400
about your corporation
to the public record.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.730
If my corporation is in the Seychelles,

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:13.660
I don't have to do any of that,

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.493
this is actually starting

00:03:14.493 --> 00:03:16.710
to seem like a pretty attractive option.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.156
These tiny nations have set up their laws

00:03:19.156 --> 00:03:22.890
to attract big corporations
for this very purpose,

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:25.180
to set up on paper in their country,

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.360
so that the government can
make a little bit of money

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.860
off of the little taxes they receive

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:32.160
and any of the registration fees and dues.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.470
And it's not just corporations,

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:36.580
the same concept applies
to shipping vessels.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.980
These are big barges that
make our world economy run,

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:42.460
and they spend most of their time in water

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.870
that belongs to no country,

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.180
and yet they still have
to follow the rules

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.630
of the country, whose flag they fly,

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:49.760
where they're registered.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:52.880
And so if you register to a
country that has very low taxes,

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.500
and no laws around how you need

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.930
to treat your employees on the boat,

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:59.410
and what safety regulations
you need to follow,

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.350
then those are the
rules you need to follow

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.770
when you're out on the high sea.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:05.190
So, the modern global economy turns out

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.170
to be a race to the bottom.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.410
Corporations and shipping vessels,

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:13.010
registering themselves to
whatever country will give them

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.310
the least amount of
accountability and transparency,

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.300
we call these havens,
tax havens or shelters.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.060
And this isn't just like
shady criminal corporations,

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:26.230
most corporations that you
interact with on a daily basis,

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:30.050
have loads of subsidiaries
in far away tax havens,

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:30.900
that they have set up

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.513
to escape transparency and accountability.

00:04:34.598 --> 00:04:37.120
(low tempo music)

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.050
- Okay, but back to me

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:41.490
and my corporation that I
theoretically want to sign up,

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.070
If I wanna set up in the Seychelles

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.750
or the British Virgin islands,

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.860
this is actually kind of complicated,

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.130
how do I navigate all the
laws and the paperwork?

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.200
Ask the internet.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.350
And when I asked the internet,
I get a bunch of ads.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.510
These are ads of companies
who are dedicated

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.530
to helping corporations set up

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.920
in these offshore jurisdictions
and these tax havens.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.570
So, if I wanna set up in
the British Virgin islands,

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.510
I could choose a bunch
of different companies

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.330
to help me get that paperwork done.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.070
And then while I actually do my business

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.420
back here in Washington, DC,

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:13.830
they help manage all the
taxes and the requirements,

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.500
and all the little things I need to do

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.360
to upkeep my little facade

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.460
of having a company in this place,

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.700
even though I actually don't.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:22.450
Okay, so here's where this gets weird,

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:25.850
we're talking about tax havens
and offshore jurisdictions

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.740
and all this stuff, let's
get back to Liberia,

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:30.590
which Liberia is one of these tax havens.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.260
It's a place that has structured its laws

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:35.070
to attract foreign corporations
and shipping vessels,

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.540
to register with them so that
they can make a little money

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.333
off of those dues and taxes.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:43.590
- [Narrator] When I go to start
my corporation in Liberia,

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.620
I don't get a bunch of ads for middlemen

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:48.260
who wanna help me set up my
new Liberian corporation,

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:51.150
instead I'm funneled to
one company, this one,

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.850
and this company boasts that
it has the exclusive right

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.210
to handle all companies
that wanna register

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.690
their corporation or ship in Liberia.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:01.550
This is the company whose
building is near my house.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.540
And on the surface, it just
looks like another middleman,

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.300
paper pusher, super boring,

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.430
but you peek under the surface

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:08.770
and there's something
way bigger going on here.

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:10.860
Not just a corporation
running away from taxes

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:11.810
and accountability,

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.200
but instead this is a symbol

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.480
of how the US projects its
power in the 21st century,

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:20.340
and how it uses other
countries to hide its secrets.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:21.960
(dramatic music)

