00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.900
Let's get back to the story of Liberia

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.840
and what the heck is happening in Liberia,

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:11.930
it gets pretty nuts from here.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:14.510
(upbeat music)

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:15.343
What's the deal?

00:09:15.343 --> 00:09:19.260
Why does this one random
building in Virginia,

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:23.110
run a network of corporate secrecy

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:24.830
in the country of Liberia?

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:25.920
Like it's so weird,

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.150
and as soon as you start to
go down this rabbit hole,

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.290
it just gets weirder.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.710
And the short answer here is that

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:35.570
the United States of
America literally invented

00:09:35.570 --> 00:09:36.960
the country of Liberia.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:40.380
Back in the 1800s here
in the United States,

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:44.320
the biggest, most important
debate was over slavery.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:48.200
This issue led the country
to almost imploding on itself

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:49.650
in a bloody civil war.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.840
During this debate,

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:54.760
there emerged three major
camps with the slavery issue.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:57.070
One where the abolitionists,
the people who were like,

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.160
dude, this is wrong,

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.910
let's reform our country

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.210
to be done with this
terrible thing we've done.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:03.950
And then of course there were the people

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.020
on the pro-slavery side,

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:07.430
who were often had a financial incentive

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:09.870
to keep slavery alive
with their plantations

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:11.080
and their businesses.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.230
But then there was this
third camp in the middle,

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.790
who were on paper against slavery.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:18.080
They wanted to get rid of
slavery, it was a bad thing,

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.350
but they didn't really want
the freed black Americans

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.110
to integrate into American society.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.790
As this debate, raged on,

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:28.420
there were some Americans here in Virginia

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:29.940
who came up with a solution.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.410
What if we gave the option

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:35.200
to enslaved people who had been freed,

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.320
to go to Africa where
their ancestors came from?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.410
We could ship them back.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:42.740
We could buy a piece of land
and they would all flock

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:45.860
to the boats to go back to
Africa was the thinking here.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.090
The quasi abolitionists
kind of liked this,

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:48.923
'cause they're like, Oh yeah,

00:10:48.923 --> 00:10:51.540
we can get the moral buzz
out of being against slavery,

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:55.400
but we don't have to deal with
the complicated consequences

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.740
of our actions to reintegrate
these people into our society.

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:01.470
And then of course the
slave owners liked this too,

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:03.930
because it meant that
any freed black Americans

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:05.130
could be shipped away,

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:08.030
so they wouldn't foment
rebellion among those enslaved

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:10.600
people who were still
working on plantations.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.450
So, there was this strange alignment

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.010
between these quasi abolitionists
and these slave owners,

00:11:15.010 --> 00:11:17.463
and they started their own organization.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.590
- [Narrator] So, this organization

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:23.380
that was based here in Virginia,

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:26.870
bought a piece of land in Western Africa,

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:30.310
with money from their supporters
and from the US government.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:33.140
And they started sending
ships full of black people

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:37.240
to this land to create a
settlement that they called Liberia

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:38.810
or land of the free.

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:40.450
They named the Capital Monrovia,

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.840
after president James Monroe,

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:45.410
who was a fierce supporter of this effort

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.173
to send away free black Americans.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.090
- Okay, so at this point,
I'm sure you're kind of like,

00:11:52.090 --> 00:11:54.400
wait a minute, what was this curve ball?

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:58.490
We went from talking about
the Seychelles and tax havens,

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:00.360
to talking about how a bunch of Virginians

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.930
started sending freed black Americans

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.320
to a piece of land in
Africa that they bought,

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.920
and this is where these two come together.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:11.940
Soon, the Liberians declare independence.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:13.100
Liberian locals,

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.830
the ones who had come
from the United States,

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.870
that started to take power

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.920
and actually be the
leaders of the country.

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:22.700
They actually started to
enact slavery of their own

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.640
in their society,

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:26.870
just like they had seen
in the United States.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:29.000
But behind the scenes of all of this,

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:31.200
the US political interests

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.390
that started this whole thing remained.

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:35.180
They had an actual building there

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:37.840
and they were actually calling the shots.

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:40.100
So Liberia was independent on paper,

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:45.100
but in reality the US had
as much influence as ever,

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.667
in their little colony in Africa.

00:12:46.667 --> 00:12:49.700
And that influence became really useful

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.007
a hundred years later.

00:12:51.007 --> 00:12:53.590
(upbeat music)

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.340
So it's a hundred years later,

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:01.680
the US just got out of world war II

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:02.970
and you have this guy,

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.420
this guy was the secretary
of state for the US,

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:06.620
which is like a foreign minister.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.180
He became a US representative at the UN,

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.800
and he was out on a diplomatic tour

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.490
that brought him to Liberia.

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:15.620
While in Liberia, this
little African nation

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.080
that was created by the United States,

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.390
and still had deep ties
to the United States,

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:23.370
he looked at the deep sea port

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:25.570
that the US had created
during world war II,

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.140
and his wheels started turning.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:29.790
He returned to the United States

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:33.030
and quickly stepped down
from his role as a diplomat.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:35.030
Harry Truman like really wanted him

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:36.380
to stick around as a diplomat,

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:40.780
but he had actually a very
strong reason to leave.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:43.030
Truman said that he had
an earnest insistence

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.300
to go do his own thing.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:47.070
This guy was a diplomat, but
he was also a businessman,

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:49.990
and what he saw during
his visit to Liberia,

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:51.610
revealed a business opportunity

00:13:51.610 --> 00:13:54.100
that he just could not leave on the table.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:57.080
So over the next year,
this ex secretary of state

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.500
started scheming with
the Liberian government.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.770
And in September, 1947,

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:05.600
he came out and announced that
he a private American citizen

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:07.960
had made a deal with
the Liberian government.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:09.690
He created a company,

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:12.600
an American based company,
based here in Virginia,

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:14.570
that was to be the exclusive middleman

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:16.860
between any international corporation

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:18.410
and the government of Liberia.

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:19.243
Basically,

00:14:19.243 --> 00:14:21.030
if anyone wanted to set up
their corporation in Liberia,

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:23.840
they would have to go through
this guy and his new company.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:26.290
He helped the Liberian
government craft laws

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.100
that would make it very attractive,

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:31.410
for people to put the
Liberian flag on their ship

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:34.430
or on their company, and
over the next few years,

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.530
this gained major traction.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:40.520
At this time, any shipping
vessel that had the American flag

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.100
or the Soviet flag,

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:45.190
would be subject to a
bunch of trade barriers,

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:47.720
that were starting to go up as
a part of this like cold war

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:49.180
between the US and the Soviets.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:51.670
This ex secretary of
state and his new company,

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:54.060
would go around and say,
"Hey, put the Liberian flag

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:54.893
on your ship,

00:14:54.893 --> 00:14:56.720
and now you can trade with
whoever the hell you want."

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.700
The Liberian registry exploded,

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:01.295
and now you had ships
flying the Liberian flag,

00:15:01.295 --> 00:15:03.760
not having to pay barely any taxes,

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:07.710
and not having to obey any
laws from the United States,

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:10.140
and being able to trade
with whomever they want,

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:13.030
because Liberia was officially
neutral in the cold war.

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:16.758
The Liberian registry was
born and it was the thriving.

00:15:16.758 --> 00:15:19.341
(upbeat music)

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.680
So in recent decades,

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:29.220
the number of ships that
register under the Liberian flag,

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:31.030
who never stepped foot
in Liberia by the way,

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:33.490
but have their flag on
their ship has grown.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:36.260
And it has become the
second most common flag

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:39.350
on international ships in the
world, only second to Panama.

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:41.270
Meanwhile, the company here in Virginia,

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:44.930
who has a monopoly over this
registry is getting super rich,

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.480
and they're giving some of those riches

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:48.810
to the Liberian government.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:51.320
But what the librarian
government does with that money

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:54.710
is actually, probably
the ugliest underbelly

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:55.766
of this whole story.

00:15:55.766 --> 00:15:58.349
(upbeat music)

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:04.520
So by the late 90s this
company's doing great,

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:07.060
Liberia is taking in a bunch of money

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:10.220
from all of the ships
registering under their flag,

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:14.500
but then this guy, Charles
Taylor becomes the president.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.850
- How can I help you on
Liberian shipping registries?

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:18.790
It's a long time since
I've been looking at them.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:23.230
- What has the registry allowed
the government of Liberia

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:25.590
to do that, that it wouldn't
be able to do otherwise?

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:28.230
- It was one of the most consistent,

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:32.230
dependable sources of revenue
for the Liberian government.

00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:33.200
That was important,

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:34.950
particularly in the Charles Taylor period

00:16:34.950 --> 00:16:37.660
when it was civil war in Liberia,

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.610
and there were no other
sources of revenue.

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:41.883
It was a war economy.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.440
- He starts taking the
money that's coming in

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.920
from all these ship and
corporation registries,

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.680
but not just to fight these wars,

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:52.820
he goes on to commit some
of the most egregious

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:55.203
crimes the world has ever seen.

00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:57.630
- I was the one myself

00:16:57.630 --> 00:16:59.660
that investigated the shipping registry.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:04.400
We found, documented, exposed
that the shipping registry,

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:08.190
that its revenues were being
diverted to purchase arms

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:10.714
and ammunition in
violation of UN sanctions.

00:17:10.714 --> 00:17:13.297
(upbeat music)

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:18.170
- And yet corporations and ships

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:20.620
that fly the Liberian flag,

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:22.890
don't even have to think about this stuff.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.840
They don't step foot in Liberia.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:28.070
They've never met Charles
Taylor or any of his people,

00:17:28.070 --> 00:17:30.050
they just go about doing their thing

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.030
and doing all of their business

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:36.750
through a nondescript
office, right near my house,

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:39.740
where a company is getting very rich

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:43.630
using Liberia as the facade,

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:46.960
but really everything
is happening right here.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.400
The money is being made right here,

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:51.680
and a little bit of that
is being sent to Liberia,

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:54.120
and Liberia is using it
to do terrible things.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:55.630
Charles Taylor eventually goes

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.020
to the International Court of Justice

00:17:57.020 --> 00:18:00.790
and gets indicted on a million
really horrible counts,

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:02.750
goes to jail for the rest of his life.

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:07.750
But the registry that helped
fund his horrible rise remains,

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:14.660
and remains as a mechanism
for helping many corporations

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:15.933
around the world,

00:18:15.933 --> 00:18:19.530
hide their secrets and
evade accountability.

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:23.130
And this connection between
these two unlikely places,

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:26.280
retains a similar purpose
as its original one.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:28.120
Way back in the 1800s,

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.350
when with the support
of the US government,

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:33.420
private interests sent away their secrets

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:35.810
and their guilt to a far away place.

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:37.670
And that hasn't really stopped happening,

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:40.190
today with the blessing
of the US government,

00:18:40.190 --> 00:18:44.090
corporations continue
to deposit their secrets

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:45.930
in this same far away place,

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.903
far away from any real accountability.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:58.460
Thank you all for watching this video,

00:18:58.460 --> 00:19:01.843
this is the type of video
